.TH NOTM-CONFIG 5 "2026-06-26" "notm 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
notm-config \- configuration file for notm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/notm/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notm
uses TOML configuration.  If the file is absent, notm starts with safe defaults
and tries to discover the user's Notmuch config from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/notmuch/default/config
or
.IR ~/.notmuch-config .
.PP
An alternate file can be selected with
.B --config
for any subcommand.  For example:
.nf
notm --config path launch
.fi
.PP
.B --config
requires the selected file to exist; only an absent default configuration file
falls back to built-in defaults.
.PP
Configuration is validated before a command or desktop window starts.  Unknown
sections and keys are errors rather than being silently ignored.  Errors name
the configuration file and the invalid key or value.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[notmuch]
database_path = "/home/alice/Mail"
default_query = "tag:inbox and not tag:trash and not tag:spam"
excluded_tags = ["trash", "spam"]

[identity]
name = "Alice Example"
primary_email = "alice@example.com"

[send]
command = "/usr/sbin/sendmail"
args = ["-t", "-oi"]
mode = "stdin_rfc5322"
.fi
.SH NORMAL OPERATION SECTIONS
.SS [notmuch]
.TP
.B database_path
Path to the Notmuch database/mail root.
If unset, notm tries to read it from the Notmuch config.
.TP
.B config_path
Path to a Notmuch config file.
.TP
.B profile
Optional Notmuch profile name.
.TP
.B default_query
Startup query.  The default is
.BR "tag:inbox and not tag:trash and not tag:spam" .
.TP
.B excluded_tags
Tags excluded from normal searches.  The default is:
.nf
["trash", "spam"]
.fi
.TP
.B open_readwrite_only_for_mutations
Keep normal search/view database opens read-only and open read-write only for
mutations.  Defaults to true and must remain true; false is not supported.
.TP
.B sync_maildir_flags_after_tag_change
Ask libnotmuch to synchronize Maildir flags after tag changes when supported.
Defaults to true.
.SS [identity]
.TP
.B name
Display name used when composing mail.
.TP
.B primary_email
Primary sender address.
.TP
.B other_email
Additional addresses used for identity matching.
.SS [ui]
.TP
.B theme
Theme preference.  Accepted values are exactly
.BR system ,
.BR light ,
or
.BR dark .
The default is
.BR system .
.B system
removes the application override and follows changes to the desktop color
preference.  The other values force a light or dark application appearance.
The saved value is used at launch; Settings
.B Apply
changes the current window immediately, while
.B Save
both applies and persists the value.
.PP
On GTK 4.20 and newer, notm also selects the display Settings color scheme and
resets that application override for
.BR system .
On every supported GTK release, a forced value uses GTK's
.B Default
theme and selects its light or dark variant so the GTK 4.12 through 4.18
fallback remains deterministic.  Returning to
.B system
resets both application settings.  Consequently, a forced value on those older
GTK releases and on newer releases intentionally does not retain an arbitrary
third-party GTK theme name.
.TP
.B page_size
Positive number of thread rows loaded per page.  The default is 100.
.TP
.B thread_preview_lines
Visual line limit for wrapped body previews in the thread list.  Values from 1
through 20 are accepted; the default is 2.  Settings
.B Apply
changes rendered rows immediately, while
.B Save
both applies and persists the value.  Setting
.B show_thread_preview
to false takes precedence and hides previews regardless of this limit.
.TP
.B layout
Window layout.  Supported values are
.BR auto ,
.BR three_pane
(or
.BR columns ),
and
.BR stacked .
.B auto
uses the side-by-side columns layout on wide windows and the stacked layout on
narrower windows.  The canonical saved value for side-by-side columns is
.BR three_pane .
The stacked layout puts the sidebar and message list side by side above the
message view.  Defaults to
.BR auto .
.TP
.B show_thread_numbers
Show thread row numbers.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_thread_dates
Show thread dates.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_thread_tags
Show thread tags.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_thread_preview
Show thread body previews.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_keybind_hints
Show shortcut hints on buttons.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B remote_images
Allow remote images globally in the visual HTML view.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B trusted_image_senders
Sender allow-list for remote images.
.TP
.B html_mode
HTML rendering preference.  Supported values are
.B sanitize_then_render_text_fallback
and
.BR visual_html_preferred .
The default is
.BR sanitize_then_render_text_fallback .
.TP
.B start_maximized
Start the window maximized.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B show_sidebar
Initial sidebar visibility.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_message_list
Initial message-list visibility.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_message_view
Initial message-view visibility.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B show_debug_panel
Start with the debug panel visible.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B custom_saved_searches
Array of saved search objects with
.B name
and
.B query
fields.
.TP
.B hidden_tag_searches
Tag-derived searches hidden from the sidebar.
.SS [send]
.TP
.B enabled
Enable sending UI.  Defaults to true.
A real send requires a configured
.B command
that accepts the generated RFC5322 message.
.TP
.B transport
Transport family.  Currently
.B external
is the only supported value.
.TP
.B command
External send command.
.TP
.B args
Arguments passed to the external send command.  When
.B mode
is
.BR command_template ,
at least one argument must contain the
.B {file}
placeholder.
.TP
.B mode
One of
.BR auto ,
.BR stdin_rfc5322 ,
.BR file_arg ,
or
.BR command_template .
.TP
.B working_dir
Optional working directory for the send command.
.TP
.B env
Environment variables for the send command.
.TP
.B timeout_seconds
Send timeout.  Defaults to 120.
.TP
.B save_sent
Save accepted sent mail to a local Maildir.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B sent_maildir
Sent Maildir path.  Defaults to
.I Sent
under the database path when sent saving is enabled.
.TP
.B sent_tags
Tags applied to indexed sent mail.  Defaults to:
.nf
["sent"]
.fi
.TP
.B index_sent_after_send
Index the saved sent file through libnotmuch after a successful send.  Defaults
to false.
.SS [drafts]
.TP
.B save_maildir
Save explicit drafts as local Maildir messages.  Defaults to true.
.TP
.B maildir
Draft Maildir path.  Defaults to
.I Drafts
under the database path when Maildir drafts are enabled.
.TP
.B tags
Tags applied to indexed draft messages.  Defaults to:
.nf
["draft"]
.fi
.TP
.B index_after_save
Index explicit draft saves through libnotmuch.  Defaults to true.
.SS [sync]
.TP
.B enabled
Master gate for manual and startup sync.  When false, notm hides the sidebar
Sync action and runs no configured sync commands.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B manual_action_label
Text shown on the sidebar Sync action.  Defaults to
.BR Sync .
.TP
.B external_receive_enabled
Make the external receive command eligible for the manual Sync action and for
startup sync when its other startup gates are satisfied.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B external_receive_command
Shell command used to fetch or synchronize mail.  It runs before the database
update command.  Defaults to an empty string, which is not runnable.
.TP
.B external_receive_on_startup
Allow the external receive command to run at startup when every other startup
gate is satisfied.  This setting does not restrict the manual Sync action.
Defaults to false.
.TP
.B notmuch_database_update_enabled
Make the database update command eligible for the manual Sync action and for
startup sync when its other startup gates are satisfied.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B notmuch_database_update_command
Shell command used to update the local Notmuch database, for example
.BR "notmuch new" .
It runs after the receive command.  Defaults to an empty string, which is not
runnable.
.TP
.B notmuch_database_update_on_startup
Allow the database update command to run at startup when every other startup
gate is satisfied.  This setting does not restrict the manual Sync action.
Defaults to false.
.PP
For the manual Sync action, each command requires
.BR enabled ,
its own
.B *_enabled
flag, and a nonblank
.B *_command
value.  At startup, each command runs only on a non-fixture launch when those
three gates and its own
.B *_on_startup
flag are all true.  Eligible receive and database-update commands run in that
order.  After the selected commands succeed, the current search is refreshed.
Fixture mode never executes configured external sync commands.
.SH TESTING AND DEBUGGING SECTIONS
.SS [automation]
The developer test harness is disabled by default.
The historical
.B [automation]
section controls its local socket path, token, screenshot directory, and
live-test gates.  This section is for development and smoke-test support, not
normal mail operation.  See
.BR notm-test-harness (7).
.TP
.B allow_live_send_test
Permit developer-test-harness sends against a non-fixture account and permit
the explicit
.B live-self-send
command.  Defaults to false.
.TP
.B allow_live_tag_test
Permit developer-test-harness tag mutations against a non-fixture database.
Defaults to false.
.PP
Fixture mode ignores configured external send and sync commands, captures sends
locally, and confines tag changes to its disposable database.
.SH LEGACY KEYS
The obsolete keys
.BR ui.confirm_destructive_tag_actions ,
.BR send.one_live_self_test_per_run ,
and
.B sync.show_manual_sync_button
are accepted for compatibility but ignored and omitted from printed
configuration.  They can be removed from existing files.  Other unknown keys
are errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notm (1),
.BR notm-test-harness (7)
